From 90c863322b656da230c694fcd1989c05ff627418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:55:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/34] demux: ogg: allow seeking once the streams have been
 torn down

At the end of a stream Demux() tears the logical streams down, and in the
single stream case parks the last one in p_old_stream so that
Ogg_BeginningOfStream() can reuse its ES. p_sys->i_streams is zero from
that point on, so Ogg_GetSelectedStream() iterates over nothing, returns
NULL, and every seek is refused with "No selected seekable stream found".

That state is reachable and seeking out of it is meaningful: the input
seeks back to the start to repeat a file, and a user can drag the seek
bar after playback has ended. Neither works, and MainLoopTryRepeat() in
particular has nothing to fall back on -- it pushes the seek, the seek
fails, EOF is still set, so it pushes it again, burning through its
repeat counter as fast as it can and writing two error lines each time.
With --input-repeat=65535 on a Vorbis file that is ten megabytes of log
and a busy loop where there should have been a repeat.

The parked stream still carries the granule/time state the seek needs,
and seeking is exactly what makes the demuxer usable again: with the read
position moved, the next Demux() re-reads the headers and starts over.
Fall back to it instead of refusing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/ogg.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/ogg.c b/modules/demux/ogg.c
index 43b0ebf046..126581eeef 100644
--- a/modules/demux/ogg.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ogg.c
@@ -759,6 +759,13 @@ static logical_stream_t * Ogg_GetSelectedStream( demux_t *p_demux )
             break;
         }
     }
+
+    /* At end of stream the logical streams are torn down and the last one
+     * is parked in p_old_stream; it still has what the seek needs. */
+    if( p_stream == NULL && p_sys->p_old_stream != NULL &&
+        p_sys->p_old_stream->p_es != NULL )
+        p_stream = p_sys->p_old_stream;
+
     return p_stream;
 }
 
